solution:
[Overview]
This is a quadratic equation problem. The goal is to find all real values of x satisfying the equation. The key idea is to expand, combine like terms, and factor the resulting quadratic.

[Plan]
P1. Expand the right-hand side.
P2. Move all terms to one side and combine like terms.
P3. Simplify the resulting quadratic equation.
P4. Factor and solve the quadratic.
P5. Verify the solution in the original equation.

[Solution]
S1. [symbolic] Expand the right side -> {{-(x+3)(x+5) => -x^2 - 8x - 15}}
S2. [symbolic] Move all terms to the left and combine -> {{x^2 + 4x + 3 - (-x^2 - 8x - 15) => 2x^2 + 12x + 18}}
S3. [symbolic] Set the combined expression equal to zero and divide by 2 -> {{2x^2 + 12x + 18 = 0 => x^2 + 6x + 9 = 0}}
S4. [symbolic] Factor the quadratic -> {{x^2 + 6x + 9 => (x+3)^2}}
S5. [theorem] A square is zero only when its base is zero.
S6. [symbolic] Solve the squared equation -> {{(x+3)^2 = 0 => x = -3}}

[Check]
V1. Substitute x = -3 into the left side -> <<(-3)^2 + 4*(-3) + 3 = 0>>
V2. Substitute x = -3 into the right side -> <<-((-3)+3)((-3)+5) = 0>>

[Answer]
\boxed{-3}

