solution:
[Overview]
This is a system of two linear equations in two variables. The goal is to find the ordered pair (u,v) satisfying both equations. The key idea is to eliminate one variable and then substitute back to find the other.

[Plan]
P1. Rewrite the equations with variables on the left.
P2. Multiply one equation to prepare for elimination of v.
P3. Add the equations to eliminate v.
P4. Solve for u.
P5. Substitute u into one original equation to solve for v.
P6. Verify the ordered pair in both original equations.

[Solution]
S1. [setup] Write the system in aligned form as 5u + 2v = -7 and 3u - 4v = -25.
S2. [symbolic] Multiply the first equation by 2 -> {{5u + 2v = -7 => 10u + 4v = -14}}
S3. [symbolic] Add the second equation to this result -> {{(10u + 4v) + (3u - 4v) = -14 + (-25) => 13u = -39}}
